Round 3 registered verdicts: one function per block (U, H, G, Q, N, X) with pairing checks

analysis/round3_registered.py judges the predictions of prereg/v4_round3.md as amended on
2026-10-16: every registered quantity with its world-clustered interval, a verdict per
prediction (holds, fails, not_judged with the reason) and the reading it triggers. U: R_refresh
and R_upsert per branch, D arm and class, U1-U5. H: amended validity from calls.jsonl, the run
summaries or the response cache; H1 reading, H2, the H-c trigger, H3 (v3 P-D1). G: G1/G2 with a
two-way bootstrap over worlds x 18 held-out definitions, G3 over worlds x program sets, the
writer share of the variance and the S_del interaction per writer. Q1/Q2. N1 wraps
ex_round3_natural.paired_vs_natural. X1 with the amended threshold over analysis.x_mem0.

Pairing: complete runs only, newest per (group, cell, world, branch), superseded copies must
agree, hash checks, probe keys and gold against the committed reference, anchor answers; any
mismatch refuses every verdict of the block. A prediction whose registered worlds are not all
present is not judged (its interim value is kept apart). CLI:
python -m memshift.analysis.round3_registered BLOCK --runs ... --compare ... --out FILE.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
